    "millsfield:images_texts": [
      "CHICAGO\nUNITED\nNEW, EASY-REFERENCE\nCITY TIMETABLE\nSee next page\nJULY 1, 1961",
      "VANCOUVER\nSEATTLE TACOMA\nPORTLAND\nMINNEAPOLIS ST. PAUL\nMILWAUKEE\nCHICAGO\n_DETROIT\nCLEVELAND\nPITTSBURGH\nOMAHA\nSACRAMENTO\nSAN FRANCISCO\nSALT LAKE CITY\nRENO\nBUFFALO\nBOSTON\nNEW YORK/NEWARK\nPHILADELPHIA\nWASHINGTON, BALTIMORE\nRICHMOND\nNORFOLK\nDENVER\nKANSAS CITY\nHONOLULU\nLAS VEGAS\nLOS ANGELES\n\\ SAN DIEGO\nMEMPHIS\nBIRMINGH\nNEW ORLEANS\nUnited flights are timed to the stars by the Elgin National Watch Company.\nMIAMI\nNOW UNITED SERVES 117 CITIES COAST TO COAST AND TO HAWAII\nTO BETTER SERVE YOU...\nA QUICK, CONVENIENT SOURCE OF FLIGHT INFORMATION\nOur new quick-reference timetable lists the most frequent\nUnited flights to and from a given area. A similar city version\nappears in many originating and connecting cities across\nUnited's system. For a complete listing of all United flights,\ncontact the nearest United Air Lines office.\nFinding the exact flight you wish to take is a quick, simple\nstep with this handy guide. Instead of searching through\nmany pages, you'll find all the information you need listed in\nThe left page lists destination cities in alphabetical order.\nThe right page lists cities of origin-also in ABC order. After\neach city listing, the \"Leave\" and \"Arrive\" times appear in\nchronological order. The flight number follows.\nPlease note also, we list additional information that can prove\nhelpful in selecting your flight...\n• days of week flight is in operation\n• number of stops en route\n• type of aircraft\n• type of meal service\n• service (First Class, etc.) and fares\n• limousine fare from city to airport\n• mileage and direction from city to terminal\nPertinent information regarding each flight is fully covered and\nwe hope you'll find this new timetable greatly simplified and\neasier to read.\nThis easy-reference timetable is another example of United\nAir Lines Extra Care in every detail of your flight."
    ],
